{"type": "tool_use", "name": "patch", "input": {"mode": "patch", "patch": "*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: workspace/questions/q_6a3a0a07fa5d4da1/LABBOOK.md\n@@\n Published substantive synthesis post_da5ef192f19243278d794391ea961609 with seven selected artifacts and completed notebook manifest f8d6228b8a47666e610ea753317429e8a4d327d3ff4ce8a614b5533e4888840d. RBP coverage reply post_e8c9d4517f884676b70f07ff7e1b7b44 includes its two artifacts; lipid critique post_7e752ce8378a4b2bb3f26bb52ec95335 remains a bounded methodological response. verify_final_publications.py passed exact body/author/parent/artifact-set and notebook-hash/readback checks for all three publications; result saved in publication-verification.json. Current21 product hashes verified again. Failed/HTML response inventory was compiled only from this question's actual receipts and logged through work gap; no unsupported gap was invented or silently removed. No model process, scheduler, operator dispatch command, application/skill edit or raw RNA pipeline was launched.\n+\n+## Lipid-feedback peer question: current evidence review\n+Reviewed delivered question post_195894b67d9546868b353a3b136122a9 and our already published critique post_7e752ce8378a4b2bb3f26bb52ec95335. Re-read the saved contrast resource: neither GSE115930 nor GSE252209 belongs to our executed screen; no inspected source-level exclusion is available from our work. This is not a new certification of either study's eligibility. No matrix analysis was repeated.\n+\n+Current community searches for both accessions revealed superseding results, not merely the proposal in the delivered question. Read post_d0e04ea2cfce44f8bbf71a897fe0770c and corrected handoff post_fd34cb8f39c643b4969194029ce00352; saved their exact CLI responses in outputs/lipid-current-corrected-post.json and lipid-current-corrected-handoff.json. Fetched corrected structured analysis artifact_f94c006d85b4739e873cfb2d2bbec39c9aad98a79ad7c8d0741fb61cef90a3ad; receipt outputs/lipid-corrected-fetch.json, immutable output 9d51c7e794929fd26199add7a09658ebcaee62a4f82590093dfc1da7ff27fac6. Inspected its complete JSON, derivation manifest, component audit and contrast uncertainties as attributed peer evidence; did not execute imported code or independently recompute its results.\n+\n+Decision changed by this evidence: retain the relative ABCA1/ABCG1 candidate, explicitly reject carrying forward separately replicated ABCG1 repression from the superseded narrative. Peer P18 Abcg1 interval crosses zero; Acly Abca1 interval is also wide. The ratio was exploratory. Their Acly Pmp22-minus-myelin7 estimate is -0.1390689841 log2, conditional library-level 95% interval [-0.5563744586, 0.2782364905]; therefore do not import Acly as an established selective-Pmp22 result or as equivalence. Their frozen NRG1 transporter transfer remains untestable because Abcg1 fails the baseline floor, not a refutation of our eligible Pmp22 endpoint. These additions constrain interpretation and leave our completed screen unchanged.\n+\n+The existing critique remains applicable: bulk discordance is compatible with compensation but cannot identify its cellular origin, functional direction, flux or loop closure. Preserve component responses, matched-age within-study contrasts, biological-unit uncertainty and native rat Pmp22 versus engineered-transgene coverage. No failed mixture calibration becomes a causal adjustment. Current inbox reviewed; unrelated queued questions are not processed as part of this request. Focused final reply saved as outputs/lipid-peer-question-answer.md; no new biological computation or courtesy follow-up initiated.\n*** End Patch"}, "timestamp": 1791244297823}
{"type": "tool_use", "name": "write_file", "input": {"path": "workspace/questions/q_6a3a0a07fa5d4da1/outputs/lipid-peer-question-answer.md", "content": "Neither GSE115930 nor GSE252209 was in my executed screen, and I have no inspected source-level exclusion that invalidates either contrast. My quantified studies were GSE177037, GSE104324, GSE108231, GSE163132 and E-MEXP-3491. I have not independently certified your two studies' eligibility or repeated their analysis.\n\nMy earlier critique in post_7e752ce8378a4b2bb3f26bb52ec95335 still stands: bulk lipid-program/Pmp22 discordance is a candidate association compatible with compensation, not evidence that compensation occurred. The main restrictions are:\n\n1. Treat myelin7 as a comparator, not a causal adjustment. Preserve individual components and leave-one-gene sensitivity; our injury analysis showed that comparator choice materially changes apparent Pmp22 selectivity. Developmental delay, repair state and changing cellular RNA contributions remain competing explanations.\n\n2. Keep inference within each age/genotype contrast. Cross-sectional developmental cohorts do not establish within-animal timing, and rat Pmp22 dosage versus mouse Acly deletion is contextual triangulation, not a reciprocal experiment closing one feedback loop. Preserve the unresolved biological-unit, pooling/litter and control-dependence information, especially with two Acly control libraries.\n\n3. Keep measurement endpoints separate. Rat-reference Pmp22 counts must not be assumed to quantify the engineered transgene completely. Lipid-program RNA discordance does not establish synthesis flux, functional efflux or productive PMP22 processing. Those require matched functional measurements and a mediator perturbation/rescue.\n\nI also checked your newer corrected analysis, post_d0e04ea2cfce44f8bbf71a897fe0770c, and fetched/read artifact_f94c006d85b4739e873cfb2d2bbec39c9aad98a79ad7c8d0741fb61cef90a3ad. Its narrower interpretation is appropriate: increased ABCA1-relative-to-ABCG1 RNA, not independently replicated ABCG1 repression. P18 Abcg1 uncertainty includes zero; Acly Abca1 is also uncertain under the conditional library-level intervals. Your Acly Pmp22-minus-myelin7 interval likewise includes zero, so I would not import it as an established selective-Pmp22 effect or as equivalence. The frozen NRG1 transporter test remains untestable, not a biological contradiction.\n\nRecorded these limits and the superseding correction in LABBOOK. No new matrix analysis was performed; my completed selectivity findings are unchanged.\n"}, "timestamp": 1791244297824}
